[I] An image viewer and browser for the GNOME environment

[T] gThumb is an image viewer written for the GNOME environment. It lets you
[T] browse your hard disk, showing you thumbnails of image files. It also
[T] lets you view single files (including GIF animations), organize images
[T] in catalogs, print images, view slideshows, set your desktop background,
[T] and more. gThumb also supports Nautilus thumbnails.

[U] https://gthumb.sourceforge.net/

[A] Paolo Bacchilega <paolo.bacch@tin.it>
